{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-30 15:10:10 GMT  \nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-30 22:10:10 +07 (+0700)  \nCoding-Agent: gpt-6-sol\n\n# DHT S1 fix round 3 report\n\nCompleted F1 and the requested Low and Info edits in the `dht-s1` worktree. The report is at [the round 4 report](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1790764302000-stream-engineer-dht-s1-raw-datagram.gpt-6-sol.report-r4.md). Nothing was staged or committed.\n\n## Changes\n\n- The JVM seam now rejects a destination whose IP family differs from `bind-host` **before sending**. It answers `transport-error` and deposits `send-failed` with reason `IP family mismatch`, including for wildcard binds.\n- Added a JVM test that binds `0.0.0.0`, checks the mismatch refusal and failure event, then verifies an IPv4 canary still arrives.\n- Renamed the JVM and Node bad-port tests to `live-socket-send-failure-preserves-canary`.\n- Documented that Dart’s asynchronous `onError` path has no direct host-error test in S1. Removed the duplicate “dropped” in §4 and the trailing whitespace in `datagram.cljc`.\n\n## Test-first evidence\n\nBefore the JVM fix, the new wildcard-bind test failed twice: sending to `::1` answered `ok` and deposited no `send-failed` event. The focused suite reported 10 tests, 55 assertions, 2 failures. After the fix, it reported **10 tests, 55 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Final checks observed\n\n- Kondo: **0 errors, 0 warnings**. Cljstyle and `git diff --check`: clean.\n- Full JVM lane: **2,440 tests, 185,174 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n- Node lane: **2,344 tests, 51,582 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors**; shadow-cljs reported 0 warnings.\n- Dart lane: **2,303 passed; all tests passed**. Babashka printed a `sysctl failed` process-cleanup exception after the green verdict; the command exited 0.\n\nThe Dart `onError` path remains without a direct host-error test, as the Architect accepted for S1. Throughput was not